(a) the humanitarian assistance, including food, medicines and relief material, provided by India to civilians affected by Gaza conflict since October, 2023;
(b) the diplomatic initiatives undertaken by India to facilitate humanitarian access, ceasefire and protection of civilians in the conflict region;
(c) India's voting pattern and official position in multilateral forums on resolutions relating to the Gaza conflict during the said period;
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of ongoing conflict on India's strategic, economic and energy interests; and
(e) the measures taken by Government to ensure the safety and evacuation of Indian nationals from the conflict-affected region?

(a) the funds allocated, released and utilised by the University Grants Commission (UGC) during last five years, year-wise;
(b) the grants released by the UGC to Central, State, Deemed and Private Universities during the said period, category-wise;
(c) whether Government has reviewed the decline in grants to State Universities, if so, the details thereof;
(d) the major policy changes made during last five years relating to the powers, autonomy and regulatory functions of the UGC, including appointment of Vice-Chancellors and higher education governance; and
(e) whether any further reforms of the UGC are under consideration?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of the operational challenges being faced by major Central Government hospitals in Delhi, including AIIMS, Safdarjung Hospital, Dr. Ram Manohar Lohia Hospital and Lady Hardinge Medical College, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the sanctioned and available capacity of ICU beds, operation theatres, diagnostic equipments (CT Scan, MRI, PET-CT, Ultrasound and other major equipments), along with the number of non-functional equipment and the average downtime during the last three years, hospital-wise; and
(c) the sanctioned strength, working strength and vacancies of doctors, specialists, nurses, technicians and other healthcare personnel in these hospitals, hospital-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of reported shortages of DAP, urea and other fertilisers in Karnataka during the ongoing Kharif season;
(b) whether Government is aware of the discrepancy between the fertiliser availability claimed by the Centre and shortages reported by the Government of Karnataka;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of global supply chain disruptions and the West Asia conflict on fertilizer availability and the contingency measures taken before Kharif season; and
(d) the steps taken to augment supplies, prevent hoarding and black marketing and ensure timely availability of fertilizers to Karnataka's farmers?

(a) the methodology currently adopted for estimation of Gross Domestic Product (GDP), Gross Value Added (GVA) and other National Accounts aggregates, including the data sources used for various sectors;
(b) whether Government has taken cognisance of concerns raised by national and international institutions regarding India's GDP estimation methodology, outdated base year, delays in data revision and inadequate coverage of the informal sector, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the present status of revision of the GDP base year and National Accounts methodology, including the proposed incorporation of GST and other administrative databases, and the timeline for implementation?
