(a) the number of petrol vehicles, E20 compatible and non-compatible across the country, vehicle-wise;
(b) whether Government has conducted independent testing regarding the impact of E20 fuel on vehicles manufactured before E20 compatibility, if so, whether the reports have been placed in the public domain;
(c) the reasons for not ensuring nationwide availability of pure petrol for owners of non-E20 compatible vehicles;
(d) whether Government has assessed the financial burden on owners of older vehicles due to the transition to E20 fuel; and
(e) the measures taken to protect consumers while implementing the ethanol blending programme?
